- content_for(:title, "Car tracking — Patrol Call System")
-# Turbo keeps no copy of this page, so Back never shows an identifier again.
- content_for(:head, tag.meta(name: "turbo-cache-control", content: "no-cache"))
.page-heading
  %h1 Car tracking
- if @key
  .flash.flash-notice.tracking-key{ role: "status" }
    %p
      %strong= @car.call_sign
      Copy the identifier now: it is shown only this once.
    %code.secret= @key
    %p In Traccar Client: Server URL #{traccar_url}, Device identifier the one above, Location accuracy: high.
%section.tracking-setup{ aria: { labelledby: "tracking-sources-title" } }
  %h2#tracking-sources-title Where each car's position comes from
  %table.data-table.compact.tracking
    %thead
      %tr
        %th{ scope: "col" } Car
        %th{ scope: "col" } Position source
        %th{ scope: "col" } Device identifier
        %th{ scope: "col" } Last position
        %th{ scope: "col" }
          %span.visually-hidden Actions
    %tbody
      - @cars.each do |car|
        = render "trackings/car", car:, position: @positions[car.id]
  %p.note A choice is saved at once.
%section.tracking-setup{ aria: { labelledby: "tracking-meaning-title" } }
  %h2#tracking-meaning-title The sources
  %p
    %strong Not tracked
    — no position is taken and the car is not shown on the map.
  %p
    %strong Traccar Client
    — the free app on the crew's phone sends the position, also with the phone locked. Server URL #{traccar_url}, the
    car's identifier, location accuracy high. An identifier is shown once and replaced by a new one; positions with any
    other identifier are refused.
  %p
    %strong Crew's phone
    — the crew screen sends the phone's position every 30 seconds while it is open; nothing comes while the phone is
    locked or another app is in front. Nothing to install.
